{"type":"message","id":"ce818e20","parentId":"8242e30c","timestamp":"2026-05-18T04:20:57.430Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, no output from grep -o \"TEST_MSG\". The message didn't get posted. The POST endpoints are all returning \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which means they're just hitting the root handler, not actually processing the send.\n\nWait, but looking more carefully - the command output shows \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" first (from the POST), then nothing from grep which means the TEST_MSG wasn't found in history. So the POST isn't actually posting anything.\n\nThe `/send` endpoint is the one that actually has a handler for POST, but it returns 500. This could mean the handler is throwing an exception due to the message content or the API key format.\n \nLet me explore what POST requests are actually supported on this platform - maybe the issue is that `/send` expects the message in a different format, like query parameters or form data instead of JSON.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-385d6b7c-beb0-4258-82dd-5c7aacf18f9c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try /send with query params instead of JSON body\ncurl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=TEST_QUERY_PARAM\" 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":25347,"output":283,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25742,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779078046197,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b7d2049e-2e68-4e82-b13e-572d49e88ab9"}}
